  "sourceObservations": {
    "druid": "Broad open hood, beige face, dark sleeves, short tunic and tall visible boots. Plain blue collar I; one green connected leaf mantle II+. Two two-prong antlers III+. Rear cape has three broad leaf tips IV+. No book, metal armor or seed stone before V.",
    "mage": "Continuous long robe, blue pointed hood/cap without brim I, broad bent wizard brim II+. Hat tip bends anatomical left and backward. One violet diamond staff. Shoulder mantle III+, navy IV/VI, slim silver edge VI. Closed book IV/V, open VI, always anatomical left.",
    "cleric": "Continuous long robe, blue open hood I, folded bishop mitre II+. One broad front stole II+. Plain gold Latin cross on wooden shaft all six. Closed book IV/V, open VI, always anatomical left. Navy shoulders IV; rank cloth shoulders others."
  },
  "inferredHiddenConstruction": {
    "bodyRobe": "Long robe is one closed editable mesh, with inferred hidden pelvis underneath; a simple front slit occurs only in Cleric I where shown.",
    "cape": "All capes are single open-front U-section physical wraps with seven cross-section landmarks and actual .018 SOLIDIFY thickness; rear/front occlusion is resolved by one garment rather than camera-specific duplicate parts. Druid short wrap: hem .50, spread .40, rearY -.43. Mage/Cleric integrated short shoulder drape: hem .50, spread .315, rearY -.315, waist section narrowed by .90. Long plain wrap: hem .22, spread .41, rearY -.49. Druid three-leaf-tip wrap: hem .14, spread .43, rearY -.52.",
    "cross": "One fixed XZ-plane Latin cross .054 deep; concept side drawings show more cross-face width than a strict true profile permits, so final construction notes take precedence. All right-hand staffs are held forward at Y=.45, about .21 ahead of the face; profile staff placement was reconciled from the measured forward separation, not treated as a drawing inconsistency.",
    "leaves": "Staff blades use a fixed XZ-plane folded broad shape with thickness .057. Reference profile leaves appear broader than their front/back thickness determines; no per-camera billboard is used.",
    "mitre": "VI two points are front/back bishop peaks, with a .115-deep crown valley. Front silhouette preserves the final PNG single apex while making the required two-point structure in depth. Earlier mitres use .042 crown valley. Crown depth narrows toward the peaks: earlier peak Y .046/-.064, VI .083/-.082, versus lower crown Y .126/-.143. One ivory/gold ribbon follows the actual tapered crown to rear as PNG shows; front-only stole never repeats at back.",
    "antlers": "Two modest antlers, each exactly two ends. Main radius tapers .040 to .016 and prong radius .034 to .014. Each fork separates in true depth: main tip Y -.110, inner-prong tip Y .075, retaining chunky fork silhouettes in both profiles without camera-facing duplicates.",
    "wizardHat": "Mage I open pointed cap reaches Z 2.015 with its peak swept to Y -.185; rear roof slopes down to Z 1.925, removing the earlier flat profile ridge. II-VI use one closed 12-section annular brim with .022 cloth thickness, rising over the face and falling behind the head. The narrow cone bends anatomical left/back from base (0,-.008,1.742) to tip (-.277,-.285,1.995), with V/VI upper cone .038 higher. Closed surfaces are recalculated then checked by positive signed volume.",
    "books": "One left holding hand, genuine two covers/page blocks, no simulated extra hand. VI fixed open volume is angled toward viewer, with its leather spine under the one left hand.",
    "rankBelt": "Mage/Cleric IV-VI belts absent in final PNG and omitted; I-III belts remain. This is a visual detail resolved from current PNG over old models."
  },
  "exclusions": [
    "podium",
    "runtime_ground_ring",
    "runtime_rank_VI_aura",
